cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived motif catalogue in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "flybrain-connectome: traceable synthetic bio-topology generation from a real brain connectome"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency toolkit that converts the real male Drosophila brain
  connectome (MaleCNS v1.0: 166,700 neurons, 124,177,617 synapses, CC-BY) into
  task-tailored multi-agent topologies while retaining per-edge provenance back
  to the source neurons and synapse classes, serialized as W3C PROV-JSON. Three
  measured advantages (traceability, structural parsimony, structural
  stability) are reported alongside two negative results (no compute advantage,
  no energy advantage) under matched controls.
authors:
  - family-names: "Lexing"
    given-names: "厉兴"
    alias: "lm203688"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lm203688/flybrain-connectome"
url: "https://github.com/lm203688/flybrain-connectome"
keywords:
  - connectome
  - drosophila
  - multi-agent
  - network-topology
  - provenance
  - W3C-PROV
  - complex-systems
  - neuroscience

